/*
Expected output:
check 7
always 7
caught boom

The inner check block has an always block and no detect block, and it raises
an error. The always block must run first, and then the same error must be
passed on to the caller, where the outer detect block catches it. Nothing
after the inner check block may run.

The action has a parameter that the always block reads, so the parameter's
value must not be overwritten while the error is held during the always
block.
*/

class Main
    action Main
        check
            Work(7)
        detect e
            output "caught " + e:GetErrorMessage()
        end
    end

    action Work(integer value)
        check
            output "check " + value
            alert("boom")
        always
            output "always " + value
        end
        output "should not get here"
    end
end
